KG42.register("rules-6383fb790dd45ff5f275c253",{"id":"05-double_auction::v141-c-R013","paper":"05-double_auction","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R013","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M02","name":"Local clearing price","process_stage":"pricing","market_meaning":"Selection of the largest breakeven buyer-seller index supplies the marginal bid and ask used to calculate the uniform clearing price $kB_{\\gamma}^P + (1 - k)S_{\\gamma}^P$. Scope: Uniform k-DA clearing-price determination for winning participants in the local P2P energy market. Condition: Offers follow the natural ordering rule; the selected index is the largest breakeven index satisfying $B_{\\gamma}^P \\geq S_{\\gamma}^P$.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function pricing.local under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["matching.counterparties","pricing.local"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R013-E001","source":"matching.counterparties","target":"pricing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R013-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-02","v141-b-g01-ev-04"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"Uniform k-DA clearing-price determination for winning participants in the local P2P energy market.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-02","v141-b-g01-ev-04"]},"x":[],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"param_k","symbol":"k","meaning":"Constant weight applied to the marginal bid price B_{\\gamma}^P in the uniform k-DA clearing price, with the complementary weight (1 - k) applied to the marginal ask price S_{\\gamma}^P.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-02","v141-b-g01-ev-04"]},{"parameter_id":"param_B_gamma_P","symbol":"B_{\\gamma}^{P}","meaning":"Bid price at the largest breakeven index \\gamma; the marginal bid used in the uniform k-DA clearing price.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["\\gamma"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-02","v141-b-g01-ev-04"]},{"parameter_id":"param_S_gamma_P","symbol":"S_{\\gamma}^{P}","meaning":"Ask price at the largest breakeven index \\gamma; the marginal ask used in the uniform k-DA clearing price.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["\\gamma"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-02","v141-b-g01-ev-04"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R013-C001","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"Selection of the largest breakeven buyer-seller index supplies the marginal bid and ask used to calculate the uniform clearing price $kB_{\\gamma}^P + (1 - k)S_{\\gamma}^P$. Scope: Uniform k-DA clearing-price determination for winning participants in the local P2P energy market. Condition: Offers follow the natural ordering rule; the selected index is the largest breakeven index satisfying $B_{\\gamma}^P \\geq S_{\\gamma}^P$.","expression":"\\gamma = \\max\\{\\, i : B_{i}^{P} \\geq S_{i}^{P} \\,\\}; \\quad \\text{clearing price} = k\\,B_{\\gamma}^{P} + (1 - k)\\,S_{\\gamma}^{P}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["matching.counterparties","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["param_k","param_B_gamma_P","param_S_gamma_P"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-02","v141-b-g01-ev-04"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-02","location":{"location_id":"src-22913ad574-p02-c2r4__v141-a-M02-clearing","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.1","anchor_text":"a y g g p s- does not exist for each auction interval. of Uniform k-DA is a variation to discriminat","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":"Table 1","image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Uniform k-DA is a variation to discriminatory k-DA where all winning participants trade at the same price. Such market clearing price is figured by first sorting offers according to the natural ordering rule and determining the largest breakeven index $\\gamma$ where $B_{\\gamma}^P \\geq S_{\\gamma}^P$. The market clearing price is then calculated as for single-unit auctions where $B_{\\gamma}^P$ and $S_{\\gamma}^P$ are the bid and ask prices at the largest breakeven index, respectively."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-04","location":{"location_id":"src-22913ad574-p02-c2r4__v141-a-M02-pricing","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.1","anchor_text":"a y g g p s- does not exist for each auction interval. of Uniform k-DA is a variation to discriminat","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":"Table 1","image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Table 1 Auction mechanisms. Uniform k-DA | Price trading buyers pay: $kB_{\\gamma}^P + (1 - k)S_{\\gamma}^P$ | Price trading sellers receive: $kB_{\\gamma}^P + (1 - k)S_{\\gamma}^P$"}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":"This is a pricing rule that computes a derived uniform clearing price from the marginal bid B_{\\gamma}^P, the marginal ask S_{\\gamma}^P and the constant weight k; it introduces no design-selection or operational-decision variable of its own. Participants' bid and ask prices are operational decisions governed by the bidding rules (e.g. v141-c-R001, v141-c-R002) and determined at the matching/clearing stage (e.g. v141-c-R003); within this pricing rule they enter only as fixed marginal inputs.","empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M02-clearing","v141-a-M02-pricing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"pricing.local","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-02","quote":"Such market clearing price is figured by first sorting offers according to the natural ordering rule and determining the largest breakeven index $\\gamma$ where $B_{\\gamma}^P \\geq S_{\\gamma}^P$. The market clearing price is then calculated as for single-unit auctions where $B_{\\gamma}^P$ and $S_{\\gamma}^P$ are the bid and ask prices at the largest breakeven index, respectively."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-04","quote":"Uniform k-DA | Price trading buyers pay: $kB_{\\gamma}^P + (1 - k)S_{\\gamma}^P$ | Price trading sellers receive: $kB_{\\gamma}^P + (1 - k)S_{\\gamma}^P$"}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"78b79318fca3bd50a0bbb7ceb54ef6a37c3d1856c94eecc6dc714c3f020b8b7d","applicability":"formalized","reason":"The source supplies an explicit expression for this rule. v141-b-g01-ev-04 gives the Uniform k-DA trading price for both buyers and sellers as kB_{\\gamma}^P + (1 - k)S_{\\gamma}^P, and v141-b-g01-ev-02 states that offers are sorted by the natural ordering rule, that the largest breakeven index \\gamma satisfies B_{\\gamma}^P \\geq S_{\\gamma}^P, and that B_{\\gamma}^P and S_{\\gamma}^P are the bid and ask prices at that largest breakeven index. The existing constraint C001 (its statement, role, members and evidence_ids preserved verbatim) is therefore transcribed with formalization_origin = source. Within this pricing rule the marginal bid B_{\\gamma}^P and marginal ask S_{\\gamma}^P enter as fixed inputs selected by the ordering/matching stage, and k enters as a constant weight, so the rule introduces no design-selection or operational-decision variable and x is empty; the participants' bid/ask choices belong to the bidding rules. B evidence for this rule is unreviewed (no source audit performed in this experiment); the supplied quotations do not restate the units of B_{\\gamma}^P/S_{\\gamma}^P nor the domain of k, so those are left unspecified rather than inferred.","bindings":[{"object_id":"param_k","node_ids":["pricing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"k is the constant weight appearing only inside the local clearing-price formula, so it binds to the pricing.local node; it originates from the pricing computation rather than from the matching edge."},{"object_id":"param_B_gamma_P","node_ids":["pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R013-E001"],"rationale":"B_{\\gamma}^P is the bid at the breakeven index selected from the ordered offers (matching.counterparties) and consumed by the price computation at pricing.local; edge E001 is exactly the matching-to-pricing link."},{"object_id":"param_S_gamma_P","node_ids":["pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R013-E001"],"rationale":"S_{\\gamma}^P is the ask at the breakeven index selected from the ordered offers (matching.counterparties) and consumed by the price computation at pricing.local; edge E001 is exactly the matching-to-pricing link."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R013-C001","node_ids":["matching.counterparties","pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R013-E001"],"rationale":"C001 selects the breakeven index \\gamma over ordered offers (matching.counterparties) and computes the uniform clearing price at pricing.local; edge E001 (matching.counterparties -> pricing.local, constraint_ids [v141-c-R013-C001]) is the relation it governs."}],"revision_requests":["The supplied quotations for this rule do not restate the units of B_{\\gamma}^P and S_{\\gamma}^P nor the domain of k; those attributes are left unspecified here and should be confirmed against the source text. B evidence supporting this rule (v141-b-g01-ev-02, v141-b-g01-ev-04) is unreviewed in this experiment."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
